{
  "_doc": "Kid-safe text rules shared by the server (SafeText.php) and the app (socialModel.ts). Keep the two copies identical: backend resources/safetext/rules.json and app src/screens/threads/safetextRules.json. Patterns are case-insensitive regex without delimiters, run on several normalised forms of the text. {CHAT}, {APPS}, {HANDLE}, {MAIL}, {SPOT} are substituted. R5: distress (self-harm about the author) and review_you + review_topics / review_phrases (hold for a person) are not blocks; see SafeText::isDistress and ::needsReview. tens/teens turn number words like 'fifty five' into digits. R6: review_exempt phrases are removed before the review check (park talk like 'what age can you ride'). R7: care_me/care_words/care_window is the broad care net (a first-person word within care_window words of a death or self-harm word; care_exempt phrases are removed first). review_exempt now swaps only the topic noun inside the phrase. R8: care_wide_* is the wide care check (Dustin-facing; on the live forum it refuses kindly too): care_me within care_wide_window words of care_wide_words, or any care_wide_extra phrase, after care_exempt. R9: care_a_exempt phrases are removed before the Tier A care net only (they stay in the wide check).",
